// DISTRIBUTED native-scatter schedule (TASK-0384) — the multi-worker
// "broaden" of the single-worker `scatter.sched.nuc` (TASK-0376) and the
// WRITE analog of the distributed gather (TASK-0373).
//
// Drives `prog.scatter.algo.nuc` (the native data-dependent WRITE
// `histogram[input[i]] <-- inc(histogram[input[i]])`). The e2e harness
// selects the algorithm from this `schedule for` path (TASK-0049.03) and
// pairs `kernels.scatter.rs` by the variant rule (TASK-0049.08), so an
// `08-histogram/distributed.scatter` cell compiles the scatter variant.
//
// The shape:
//   host    — owns I/O (load_input / save_output) and the cross-worker
//             partial-histogram combine.
//   w0..w3  — each compute worker owns a DISJOINT i-band of `input`
//             (the outer `i` loop is the partition axis) and scatters
//             that slice into its OWN PRIVATE full-width partial
//             histogram (`let mut histogram: Vec<i32> = vec![0; 16]`).
//
// Why this is sound (the TASK-0384 soundness boundary). The partition is
// over the INPUT INDEX `i`, NOT over histogram bins. Each worker holds
// the FULL `histogram` (whole-array replicate, because its write index
// `input[i]` is data-dependent → opaque dim in
// `transfer_inject::record_access_per_dim` → whole-array broadcast), so
// a scatter to ANY bin lands in that worker's private partial. The host
// then sums the four partials ELEMENT-WISE (TASK-0343
// `collect_accumulate_waits` + `render_wait_assign(accumulate)`:
// `histogram[k] = histogram[k].wrapping_add(partial_w[k])`). That sum
// equals the single-worker histogram exactly: every input element is
// counted once, in exactly one worker's band, into the correct bin.
//
// A BIN partition (a worker owning only a band of `histogram`) would be
// UNSOUND for this replicate-then-sum shape — a worker would silently
// drop every scatter that lands outside its band. The compiler keeps
// that shape FATAL: the halo `is_scatter_rmw` gate
// (`error_is_fatal_under_partition` →
// `scatter_target_replicates_whole_array`) admits a scatter RMW under
// partition ONLY when no partitioned iv affinely indexes the scatter
// target. `prog.scatter.algo.nuc` has only the iv `i` (indexing the
// SOURCE `input[i]`), so `histogram` is never affinely banded — the
// admit shape.
//
// Cross-worker edges:
//   input      host -> { w0..w3 }   (host loads, each worker consumes
//                                    its i-band)
//   histogram  { w0..w3 } -> host   (workers produce full-width
//                                    partials, host element-wise-sums)
//
// All `sync` transfers. Verified byte-identical to `reference.bin` and
// bit-identical cross-backend on all 7 tier-1 backends (TASK-0384),
// including BOTH strict-FIFO backends (mp-tcp-bufsync AND mp-tcp-poll):
// `input` is the only host->worker broadcast and there is no
// gather-index array, so the Push/Wait FIFO order trap
// (project-mp-tcp-event-vs-bufsync-safety-profile / TASK-0389) does NOT
// bite here.

schedule for "../prog.scatter.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // I/O + cross-worker combine on host.
    place load_input  on host;
    place save_output on host;

    // The pure per-hit increment distributed across the compute workers.
    place inc on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Outer loop is the partition axis; one i-band per compute worker.
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // Cross-worker data — one transfer per data symbol that crosses.
    // `input` i-bands to each worker; `histogram` replicates whole-array
    // (data-dependent write index ⇒ opaque dim ⇒ whole-array broadcast)
    // and the partials are element-wise-summed at the host.
    transfer input     : sync;
    transfer histogram : sync;
}
